[{:db/id 17592186068915 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a41efe2e-217f-5d4e-8c40-c317692d2ec6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068916 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a6be6fa7-2d6e-5c8a-ab1e-bb035341f649" "question-66f3c3b9-c1e9-58f7-9604-16a02027760f"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186068918 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-305ab7d8-b9f8-5861-8b01-dd9a503b80df"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a41efe2e-217f-5d4e-8c40-c317692d2ec6" :question/id #uuid "a41efe2e-217f-5d4e-8c40-c317692d2ec6" :question/math-academy-id "q-10574" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=3x+\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /3$ | $2\\pi /3$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u{|}_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bcc8d1e8-f376-53d7-9c0f-65db14888af4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bcc8d1e8-f376-53d7-9c0f-65db14888af4" :answer-field/id #uuid "bcc8d1e8-f376-53d7-9c0f-65db14888af4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4952b9e8-bbdc-5ebd-87ec-3e2a8e0abe98" :answer-field/choices ["answer-027cbe6b-cc9e-5232-a368-f7d9b5981f38" "answer-4952b9e8-bbdc-5ebd-87ec-3e2a8e0abe98" "answer-d0f5b679-6496-55a2-9c95-8d9e7d1b6239" "answer-c99d3fe5-21ad-5042-83f6-cbfa8e3c7e98" "answer-d6fa740d-7171-561d-a05a-6cdf9a71c7c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027cbe6b-cc9e-5232-a368-f7d9b5981f38" :answer/id #uuid "027cbe6b-cc9e-5232-a368-f7d9b5981f38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4952b9e8-bbdc-5ebd-87ec-3e2a8e0abe98" :answer/id #uuid "4952b9e8-bbdc-5ebd-87ec-3e2a8e0abe98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0f5b679-6496-55a2-9c95-8d9e7d1b6239" :answer/id #uuid "d0f5b679-6496-55a2-9c95-8d9e7d1b6239" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c99d3fe5-21ad-5042-83f6-cbfa8e3c7e98" :answer/id #uuid "c99d3fe5-21ad-5042-83f6-cbfa8e3c7e98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6fa740d-7171-561d-a05a-6cdf9a71c7c4" :answer/id #uuid "d6fa740d-7171-561d-a05a-6cdf9a71c7c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a6be6fa7-2d6e-5c8a-ab1e-bb035341f649" :question/id #uuid "a6be6fa7-2d6e-5c8a-ab1e-bb035341f649" :question/math-academy-id "q-10578" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=x-\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\pi /3$ | $\\pi /6$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡u{|}_{-\\pi /3}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f070068b-56d2-50d4-88fa-ab05a0ca7204"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f070068b-56d2-50d4-88fa-ab05a0ca7204" :answer-field/id #uuid "f070068b-56d2-50d4-88fa-ab05a0ca7204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-02192a18-96df-5c9c-86d1-fd39f10cc96d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-605c38a6-bd94-5054-abeb-196bc585d8b9" "answer-258b40a9-d7f7-5e38-ab76-8707b1a1a9b7" "answer-02192a18-96df-5c9c-86d1-fd39f10cc96d" "answer-f513628d-4c08-512b-85ac-0d46df6f115b" "answer-59c2d43f-3033-53cf-a498-afe18808b478"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-605c38a6-bd94-5054-abeb-196bc585d8b9" :answer/id #uuid "605c38a6-bd94-5054-abeb-196bc585d8b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-258b40a9-d7f7-5e38-ab76-8707b1a1a9b7" :answer/id #uuid "258b40a9-d7f7-5e38-ab76-8707b1a1a9b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02192a18-96df-5c9c-86d1-fd39f10cc96d" :answer/id #uuid "02192a18-96df-5c9c-86d1-fd39f10cc96d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f513628d-4c08-512b-85ac-0d46df6f115b" :answer/id #uuid "f513628d-4c08-512b-85ac-0d46df6f115b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59c2d43f-3033-53cf-a498-afe18808b478" :answer/id #uuid "59c2d43f-3033-53cf-a498-afe18808b478" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-66f3c3b9-c1e9-58f7-9604-16a02027760f" :question/id #uuid "66f3c3b9-c1e9-58f7-9604-16a02027760f" :question/math-academy-id "q-355818" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /20}^{\\pi /10}5{csc}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=5x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\pi /20$ | $\\pi /10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\pi /4$ | $\\pi /2$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /20}^{\\pi /10}5{csc}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}5{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}{csc}^{2}⁡(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(u){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4b1c21c-bb6c-5c53-b4e6-f6635e6c2be4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4b1c21c-bb6c-5c53-b4e6-f6635e6c2be4" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4b1c21c-bb6c-5c53-b4e6-f6635e6c2be4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bde6a22f-af92-5d05-a00e-ee43025b38b1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bde6a22f-af92-5d05-a00e-ee43025b38b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bde6a22f-af92-5d05-a00e-ee43025b38b1" :answer/id #uuid "bde6a22f-af92-5d05-a00e-ee43025b38b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-305ab7d8-b9f8-5861-8b01-dd9a503b80df" :question/id #uuid "305ab7d8-b9f8-5861-8b01-dd9a503b80df" :question/math-academy-id "q-113997" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u={sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}(u-1)\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{u})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =u-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=C+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5edcce3e-e53a-5f19-ab28-fc88ce15b3a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5edcce3e-e53a-5f19-ab28-fc88ce15b3a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "5edcce3e-e53a-5f19-ab28-fc88ce15b3a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9f63075a-1c8a-5a7b-92d3-a38ee960a89e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e5262af-da0e-5a59-8704-7c9dacf4de2f" "answer-f18bdd3d-8085-5e2e-822e-62d75b040c5c" "answer-9fd0f034-ce27-5ace-8026-4eaf6cb1ce68" "answer-9f63075a-1c8a-5a7b-92d3-a38ee960a89e" "answer-f602ed78-2e15-5cdc-81a3-3dc36a33f074"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e5262af-da0e-5a59-8704-7c9dacf4de2f" :answer/id #uuid "5e5262af-da0e-5a59-8704-7c9dacf4de2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡x}{2}-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f18bdd3d-8085-5e2e-822e-62d75b040c5c" :answer/id #uuid "f18bdd3d-8085-5e2e-822e-62d75b040c5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fd0f034-ce27-5ace-8026-4eaf6cb1ce68" :answer/id #uuid "9fd0f034-ce27-5ace-8026-4eaf6cb1ce68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-1)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f63075a-1c8a-5a7b-92d3-a38ee960a89e" :answer/id #uuid "9f63075a-1c8a-5a7b-92d3-a38ee960a89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f602ed78-2e15-5cdc-81a3-3dc36a33f074" :answer/id #uuid "f602ed78-2e15-5cdc-81a3-3dc36a33f074" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{tan}⁡x|+K" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186320651 :answer-field/correct "answer-bf2617d8-6d99-5cd0-a36b-cb5a85fa00c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf2617d8-6d99-5cd0-a36b-cb5a85fa00c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf2617d8-6d99-5cd0-a36b-cb5a85fa00c5" :answer/id #uuid "bf2617d8-6d99-5cd0-a36b-cb5a85fa00c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070016 :tutorial/content "We know how to integrate $\\cos{x}.$ But how do we integrate $\\cos{3x}?$ \n\nTo compute\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos{3x} \\, \\textrm dx,\n$$\n\nwe can use substitution. If we let $u=3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** After solving an integral using substitution, we should always double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x+C) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186070017 :tutorial/content "Suppose that we want to calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 2x \\cos{(x^2)}\\,\\textrm d x.$\n\nNotice that if we let $u = x^2,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\underbrace{2x}_{u'} \\cos({\\overbrace{x^2}^u})\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nIn other words, the factor multiplying the trigonometric function is the derivative of the argument! Integrals like this can always be solved using substitution.\n\nSo, let $u=x^2.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d} u}{\\textrm{d}x } = 2x \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d u = 2x\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186069001 :activity/expected-seconds 1500.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
